codemap 9
tour feature-palette
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note Press ctrl+p and a box opens near the top of the window with a search field. Typing lists what matches, ranked: the tours, the steps of the tour being read, the views, the actions the registry offers to the palette (save, collapse all, hide all code, fit graph, split panel, go back...), and once something is typed every symbol and file. Each row has a kind tag, actions show their key chord. Up and down move, enter goes to the entry or runs it, a click does the same, esc or ctrl+p closes. A leading > keeps only actions. The reader needs it because reaching a symbol meant switching to the Symbols tab and filtering, and most actions are toolbar buttons that are only on screen in their own view; with the palette anything named is a few keystrokes away, and the action rows teach their chords.

